  "claim_boundary": "This v1.1 post-release pre-endpoint protocol amendment retains the frozen formal v4 checkpoint, exact v1 preflight weights, search and QAOA budgets, seeds, profile, five arms and endpoints. It corrects only the predeclared accounting of arm-independent zero-action direct roots after the first v1 attempt failed before producing any trial row, endpoint, comparison or performance outcome. The evaluation covers all forward ASCON and PRESENT S-box coordinates and is not researcher-blinded because the standards and tables were previously audited. Results are synthetic-profile effect estimates only; five ASCON coordinate clusters do not support a conventional two-sided 5% superiority test. No hardware execution, noisy-performance evidence, quantum speedup or quantum-advantage claim is made."
